Memory in WebAssembly

WASM uses:

Linear Memory

Imagine:

+----------------+
| Byte 0         |
| Byte 1         |
| Byte 2         |
| Byte 3         |
| ...            |
+----------------+

Memory is represented as:

ArrayBuffer

JavaScript can access it.

Example:

const memory = new WebAssembly.Memory({
    initial: 10
});